      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "ὁ γὰρ ἐπερωτῶν ψευδοπροφήτην περὶ πράξεώς τινος εἰδωλολάτρης ἐστὶ καὶ κενὸς ἀπὸ τῆς ἀληθείας καὶ ἄφρων.",
          "english_quote": "for the one who consults a false prophet about any matter is an idolater, empty of the truth and foolish.",
          "issue": "“About any matter” makes the condemnation unrestricted as to subject matter. The selected Greek specifies a πράξις—an action, undertaking, or affair. Although “matter” can sometimes denote an affair, the unrestricted English wording also encompasses subjects unrelated to action and conceals the source's stated scope. The theological metadata itself more accurately describes consultation “about actions.”",
          "suggested_revision": "Consider “for the one who consults a false prophet about an undertaking is an idolater, empty of the truth and foolish,” or another rendering that explicitly preserves the action/affair scope. Retain the categorical condemnation without adding exceptions. Review the replacement afresh.",
          "severity": "major"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "καὶ ἔντευξις γένηται πρὸς τὸν Θεὸν τῆς συναγωγῆς τῶν ἀνδρῶν ἐκείνων",
          "english_quote": "\"source_word\": \"ἔντευξις\", \"chosen\": \"petition\", \"alternatives\": [\"entreaty\", \"prayer\"]",
          "issue": "The lexical audit records “petition” as the chosen rendering, but the supplied reader text uses “intercession” in both paragraphs 9 and 14. “Intercession” is not even recorded among the alternatives. This is a concrete mismatch between the translation and its terminology documentation, not an objection to either synonym.",
          "suggested_revision": "Update the lexical decision to document the actual rendering “intercession” and its contextual rationale, or submit a separately reviewed reader-text change. Do not describe “petition” as the published choice while retaining the present text.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "edition": "simplified",
      "verdict": "revise",
      "checks": {
        "complete_coverage": true,
        "no_added_claims": false,
        "names_and_negations": true,
        "speaker_attribution": true,
        "source_choices_and_notes": true,
        "terminology_policy": false
      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "ὁ γὰρ ἐπερωτῶν ψευδοπροφήτην περὶ πράξεώς τινος εἰδωλολάτρης ἐστὶ καὶ κενὸς ἀπὸ τῆς ἀληθείας καὶ ἄφρων.",
          "english_quote": "Anyone who consults a false prophet about any matter is an idolater, empty of truth and foolish.",
          "issue": "Independently of the standard edition, this wording broadens consultation concerning an action, undertaking, or affair into consultation concerning absolutely any subject. The categorical assertion is preserved, but its specified action/affair scope is not explicit.",
          "suggested_revision": "Consider “Anyone who consults a false prophet about an undertaking is an idolater, empty of truth and foolish.” Review an accessible action/affair rendering afresh; do not soften the assertion or introduce doctrinal exceptions.",
          "severity": "major"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "ὅσοι οὖν ἰσχυροί εἰσιν ἐν τῇ πίστει τοῦ Κυρίου ἐνδεδυμένοι τὴν ἀλήθειαν",
          "english_quote": "Those who are strong in the Lord’s faith have put on the truth.",
          "issue": "“The Lord’s faith” naturally attributes the faith to the Lord as its possessor or exercising subject. Here the clause describes the people's strength in faith relating to the Lord. Simplification has introduced a misleading possessive formulation rather than making that relationship clearer.",
          "suggested_revision": "Consider “Those who are strong in faith in the Lord have put on the truth.” If a different understanding of the genitive is retained, document that interpretation and preserve an appropriate alternative. The proposed wording requires fresh review.",
          "severity": "major"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "καὶ ἔντευξις γένηται πρὸς τὸν Θεὸν τῆς συναγωγῆς τῶν ἀνδρῶν ἐκείνων",
          "english_quote": "\"source_word\": \"ἔντευξις\", \"chosen\": \"petition\", \"alternatives\": [\"entreaty\", \"prayer\"]",
          "issue": "The simplified edition's lexical record claims “petition,” whereas its own paragraphs 9 and 14 use “intercession.” Its metadata must document its actual translation rather than inherit an inaccurate choice record.",
          "suggested_revision": "Record “intercession” as the actual choice with a contextual rationale, or propose and freshly review a reader-text change. Also reconcile other inherited choice labels with this edition's actual wording, including “double‑minded” versus “waver” and “Deity” versus “divinity.”",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Both editions were reviewed independently against all 21 paragraphs of the selected working Greek. Both cover the argument, preserve its principal negations and difficult assertions, follow reader-facing servant policy, and disclose the contextual change-of-mind reading with repentance as an alternative. The notes adequately distinguish the retained working supplements and corrections from the reported alternatives; the supplied reports do not warrant manuscript authentication or exhaustive-collation claims. Revision is needed for the consultation scope and inaccurate terminology documentation, with an additional misleading faith formulation in the simplified edition. Suggested replacements are proposals, not accepted translations."
}
